+\paragraph{Refusal concentration and teacher truncation.}
+The audit distinguishes identical-string responses ($247/1000$), short responses ($450/1000$), refusal-prefixed responses ($621/1000$), and refusals among short responses ($448/450$). These output-defined categories overlap and are not interchangeable. Gains in a refusal subgroup do not identify a Nash-specific mechanism.
+
+Teacher truncation affects $26{,}790/84{,}000=31.89\%$ of candidate occurrences; prompt truncation affects one occurrence. Among truncated responses, the reported median loss is $232$ tokens and the observed response fraction is $61\%$. The latter quantities must retain their aggregation definitions. This is a response-tail visibility issue for the implemented teacher. The planned instruction panel therefore uses a natively supported longer-context encoder and a separate full-response evaluator, rather than increasing RoBERTa's length limit. Reported joint-positive rates $0.725/0.730$ are archived with their unit unresolved; they are not population IR certificates.
